 Now, on to the news of the day:
 
 Changes from version 3.65 -> 3.70:
 ~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~
 - Tweaked chat mode for smoother operation
 - Added EMAIL scan at logon
 - Stabalized message search functions (!)
 - New commands in message areas 
 - Command stacking with full recursion
 - New commands in file areas including global search
 - Nearly total rewrite of file areas so they work properly :)
 - HEAVY work on ShadoeMAN (BBS manager utility)
 - Speedup for msg importing with ShadoeQWK (now 8 msgs/sec)
 - Added delaytime variable for non-mnp modems :)
 - Added timeout function :)
 - Added logging of all xfer functions :)
 - BBS now requires locked serial port speed (not my fault!!)
 - Reworking of error trapping for better raliability
 - General overhaul of entire BBS code for stability
 - Added U)pload option to message areas for uploading .rep packets...

 This version, when released (23/01/95) represents the most
stable version to date. It is a MAJOR improvement over past
releases. I suggest everyone give it a look to see what its all
about. UUCP implementation is well underway, and AREXX seems to
be stable, need to test a little more before including in release.
 Interest in the bbs is still growing. We now have users on
3 continents and in 7 different countries! I know that this
isn't the best software out there yet, but it is growing rapidly,
and soon it will tower over anything it is put up against.
 
 -- I have decided, after some prodding, to include a PRELIMINARY
    version of ShadoeMAN, a BBS setup & management utility.
    It is still shaky, most functions do not work yet, but the
    initial setup portion should work fine (works here). DO NOT
    ENTER trailing slashes after DOS paths, if you have nested
    directories, the directory above must be created before ShadoeMAN
    will be able to create the underlying one. ie if you have a msg
    area with a path of 'shadoegate:message/test' , shadoegate: and
    shadoegate:message must exist prior to using ShadoeMAN....
    Like I said, it wasnt my idea to include it just yet....the initial
    setup function works fine, but use it at your own risk! It will
    output a file called 'test.config' , which, after you check that
    everything is OK, you should rename to 'config.dat' .... it will
    also create all necessary directories, provided that the above
    conditions are met. It will also install last read message pointers
    for all message areas. Good luck!


 FidoNet support is underway. I have set up my hub over here to
